Evaluating $\dfrac{dy}{dx}$ at $\blueD{\theta = \dfrac{5\pi}{6}}$ gives us the slope of our tangent line.

$\begin{align}
\greenD{\left. \dfrac{dy}{dx}\right| _{\theta=\tfrac{5\pi}{6}}}&=\dfrac{2\sin\left(2\left(\blueD{\dfrac{5\pi}{6}}\right)\right)+\cos\left(\blueD{\dfrac{5\pi}{6}}\right)}{2\cos\left(2\left(\blueD{\dfrac{5\pi}{6}}\right)\right)-\sin\left(\blueD{\dfrac{5\pi}{6}}\right)} 
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2\sin\left(\dfrac{5\pi}{3}\right)+\cos\left({\dfrac{5\pi}{6}}\right)}{2\cos\left(\dfrac{5\pi}{3}\right)-\sin\left({\dfrac{5\pi}{6}}\right)} 
\\\\
&=\dfrac{2\left(-\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}\right)-\dfrac{\sqrt{3}}{2}}{2\left(\dfrac{1}{2}\right)-\dfrac{1}{2}} 
\\\\
&=\greenD{-3\sqrt{3}}
\end{align}$
